cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  akribia: a single-engine testbed for precision-weighted models of autism,
  ADHD, and persistent post-concussion symptoms
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: London
    family-names: Chowdhury
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-2895-2857"
    email: Londopy@protonmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      General Engineering Program, College of Engineering, California
      Polytechnic State University, San Luis Obispo
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Londopy/akribia"
url: "https://londopy.github.io/akribia/"
abstract: >-
  An open-source testbed in which a single precision-weighted Bayesian
  inference engine is parameterised by one six-field configuration object, so
  that autism, ADHD and persistent post-concussion symptoms are represented
  purely as different numbers passed to the same engine, with no per-condition
  code path in the numerical core. Ships a Rust core with a pure-Python
  fallback, five discriminating tasks, and six literature-derived predictions
  encoded as executable assertions. A research and replication tool, not a
  diagnostic instrument; it runs entirely on synthetic data and has not been
  validated against patient data.
keywords:
  - computational-psychiatry
  - predictive-coding
  - bayesian-inference
  - precision-weighting
  - autism
  - adhd
  - post-concussion-syndrome
version: 0.1.3
date-released: "2026-08-04"
